<%= content_for :title, "Admin Help" %>
<%= render "admin/shared/page_header",
           title: "Admin Help",
           description: "A quick guide to running your tree recycling fundraiser." do %>
  <%= link_to "Back to Settings", admin_settings_path, class: admin_button_class(variant: :secondary) %>
<% end %>

<div class="flex max-w-5xl flex-col gap-6">
  <section class="admin-panel border border-line bg-surface dark:border-line-dark dark:bg-surface-dark" id="marketing">
    <div class="admin-panel-header border-line dark:border-line-dark">
      <div>
        <h2 class="admin-panel-title text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">Marketing</h2>
        <p class="admin-panel-description text-ink-soft dark:text-ink-soft-dark">Invite past participants to make a reservation.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="admin-panel-body space-y-4 text-ink-soft dark:text-ink-soft-dark">
      <p>Use <strong class="text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">Marketing</strong> to manage contacts and the two campaign emails: one announces that reservations are open, and the other reminds people before the deadline. Review and publish each template, then send a test. Each Send click queues one batch; after it finishes, click Send again for the next batch. Unsubscribed contacts are skipped.</p>
      <p>Marketing email requires completed email settings and <strong class="text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">Enable Email</strong>. Closing an event clears the campaign sent dates for remaining contacts so both emails can be used again next year.</p>
      <p class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-2">
        <%= link_to "Open Marketing", admin_marketing_index_path, class: admin_link_class %>
        <%= link_to "Email settings", admin_settings_section_path("email"), class: admin_link_class %>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="admin-panel border border-line bg-surface dark:border-line-dark dark:bg-surface-dark" id="reservations">
    <div class="admin-panel-header border-line dark:border-line-dark">
      <div>
        <h2 class="admin-panel-title text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">Taking reservations</h2>
        <p class="admin-panel-description text-ink-soft dark:text-ink-soft-dark">Open signups, review addresses, and prepare pickup routes.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="admin-panel-body space-y-4 text-ink-soft dark:text-ink-soft-dark">
      <p>Set the pickup dates and signup deadline, then turn on <strong class="text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">Enable Reservations</strong> under <strong class="text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">The Event</strong>. Residents enter their contact and pickup details, choose a donation option, and receive a confirmation email when email is enabled and the confirmation template is published.</p>
      <p>Use <strong class="text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">Reservations</strong> to review signups, edit or cancel reservations, verify addresses that need attention, and assign routes. With Location Services configured, addresses can be verified and routed automatically; otherwise, assign routes manually.</p>
      <p>Turn off <strong class="text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">Enable Reservations</strong> at the deadline and when pickups begin; the deadline does not close signups automatically. Use <strong class="text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">Pickup notice</strong> in System settings to replace the home-page form with your event contact details.</p>
      <p class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-2">
        <%= link_to "View reservations", admin_reservations_path, class: admin_link_class %>
        <%= link_to "Event settings", admin_settings_section_path("event"), class: admin_link_class %>
        <%= link_to "Location Services", admin_settings_section_path("location_services"), class: admin_link_class %>
        <%= link_to "System settings", admin_settings_section_path("system"), class: admin_link_class %>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="admin-panel border border-line bg-surface dark:border-line-dark dark:bg-surface-dark" id="donations">
    <div class="admin-panel-header border-line dark:border-line-dark">
      <div>
        <h2 class="admin-panel-title text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">Collecting donations</h2>
        <p class="admin-panel-description text-ink-soft dark:text-ink-soft-dark">Accept card donations online or cash and checks at pickup.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="admin-panel-body space-y-4 text-ink-soft dark:text-ink-soft-dark">
      <p>Residents can donate by card, choose cash or check at pickup, or continue without donating. Card payments require Stripe to be enabled and configured, including its webhook. Completed online donations are then recorded automatically.</p>
      <p>Use <strong class="text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">Donations</strong> to review Stripe donation records and <strong class="text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">Analytics</strong> for paid-donation totals. Your pickup crew collects any cash or checks left with trees; those amounts are not entered into Donations automatically.</p>
      <p class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-2">
        <%= link_to "View donations", admin_donations_path, class: admin_link_class %>
        <%= link_to "View analytics", admin_analytics_path, class: admin_link_class %>
        <%= link_to "Donation settings", admin_settings_section_path("donations"), class: admin_link_class %>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="admin-panel border border-line bg-surface dark:border-line-dark dark:bg-surface-dark" id="pickups">
    <div class="admin-panel-header border-line dark:border-line-dark">
      <div>
        <h2 class="admin-panel-title text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">Day-of-event pickups</h2>
        <p class="admin-panel-description text-ink-soft dark:text-ink-soft-dark">Give drivers their routes and follow pickup progress.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="admin-panel-body space-y-4 text-ink-soft dark:text-ink-soft-dark">
      <p>Before pickup day, set up zones, routes, and drivers; assign reservations to routes; enable the Pickups Portal; and give drivers its shared password. Drivers use the portal to mark each stop as <strong class="text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">Picked up</strong> or <strong class="text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">Missing</strong>.</p>
      <p>Organizers can follow progress in <strong class="text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">Pickups</strong>, use the map, or print the pickup report.</p>

      <div class="border-t border-line pt-4 dark:border-line-dark">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">When a pickup is flagged as missing</h3>
        <p class="mt-2">The stop remains on the driver&apos;s pickup list so it can be revisited. If missing-tree notifications are enabled for the reservation, a resident with a mobile number receives a text when SMS is enabled and configured. Without a mobile number, the resident receives an email when email is enabled and configured, and the missing-tree template is published. There is no automatic email fallback if a text cannot be sent.</p>
        <p class="mt-2">If the stop is later changed to Pending Pickup or Picked Up and then marked Missing again, the follow-up message is sent.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="border-t border-line pt-4 dark:border-line-dark">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">Monitor replies throughout pickup day</h3>
        <p class="mt-2">Watch the navigation badges and check <strong class="text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">SMS</strong> for texts and <strong class="text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">Mail</strong> for email replies if inbound email is configured. With outbound-only email, monitor your email provider&apos;s inbox instead. Opening a conversation or message clears its unread indicator. A reply does not change the reservation automatically.</p>
        <p class="mt-2">If a resident says the tree has been put back out, make sure the reservation still has a route, change its status from <strong class="text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">Missing</strong> to <strong class="text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">Pending Pickup</strong>, and tell the driver to return.</p>
      </div>

      <p class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-2">
        <%= link_to "Pickup overview", admin_pickups_path, class: admin_link_class %>
        <%= link_to "Missing reservations", admin_reservations_path(status: "missing"), class: admin_link_class %>
        <%= link_to "SMS inbox", admin_sms_path, class: admin_link_class %>
        <%= link_to "Email inbox", admin_mail_received_emails_path, class: admin_link_class %>
        <%= link_to "Pickups Portal settings", admin_settings_section_path("pickups"), class: admin_link_class %>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="admin-panel border border-line bg-surface dark:border-line-dark dark:bg-surface-dark" id="closing-event">
    <div class="admin-panel-header border-line dark:border-line-dark">
      <div>
        <h2 class="admin-panel-title text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">Closing the event</h2>
        <p class="admin-panel-description text-ink-soft dark:text-ink-soft-dark">Prepare for the next fundraiser after all pickups and donations are finished.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="admin-panel-body space-y-4 text-ink-soft dark:text-ink-soft-dark">
      <p>Closing an event is a permanent cleanup step, not the same as turning off reservations. It copies only name, email, mobile, and street from eligible reservations—including missing and cancelled ones—into Contacts. Unfinished signups are not copied. It then deletes every reservation, removes contacts past the retention limit, and clears marketing campaign sent dates for the next event.</p>
      <p>Donations and logs remain but lose their reservation links. Routes, drivers, settings, and other setup remain. Closing does not turn off reservations, disable the Pickups Portal, or set the next event&apos;s dates.</p>
      <p><strong class="text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">This cannot be undone.</strong> Download a backup before closing. Only admins can change retention or close the event, and must type <strong class="text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">CLOSE</strong> to confirm.</p>

      <div class="border-t border-line pt-4 dark:border-line-dark" id="retention">
        <h3 class="font-semibold text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">Contact retention</h3>
        <p class="mt-2"><strong class="text-ink dark:text-ink-dark">Current retention: <%= pluralize(@setting.contact_retention_months, "month") %>.</strong></p>
        <p class="mt-2">When the event closes, contacts created more than this many months ago are deleted. Contacts copied from the current event are new and stay. You can change the retention length on the Close Event page before confirming.</p>
      </div>

      <p class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-4 gap-y-2">
        <%= link_to "Review Close Event", admin_close_event_path, class: admin_link_class %>
        <%= link_to "Backups and data", admin_data_path, class: admin_link_class %>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="<%= admin_notice_class(:info) %>">
    <p class="admin-notice-title">More information</p>
    <p>For installation, service configuration, deployment, and technical details, visit the <%= link_to "GitHub repository", "https://github.com/carsoncole/scout-tree-recycle", target: "_blank", rel: "noopener", class: admin_link_class %>.</p>
  </div>
</div>
